  "game": "elvis",
  "notes": "Boot elvis (5.00) with four balls on trough switches 11-14 and the stacking opto 15 at 0, built-in mechanisms off. Insert three coins on the center slot (public 5), press Start (54), emulate the serve (trough position 11 empties, the ball rests on the shooter lane switch 16, leaves it and passes the shooter lane exit 10), close each playfield switch once with a 3 s gap so every output response is attributable to one closure, knock the five ELVIS drop targets down in turn and leave them down until the reset, rest a ball in the center and top saucers and on the hotel post switch, hold each flipper input (84, 82, 88, then 82 with 88), and drain the ball. The scenario never writes 33: LibPinMAME's elvis.c writes it from its own count of the stepper phases, so every level of 33 in this run is the emulator's.",
